# AI Predictor — Game Status Tabs + Final Scores + Date Filter Fix

## Overview

Two features are requested:

1. **Game Status Tabs** — Categorize matches into three selectable tabs: **Upcoming**, **In-Play**, and **Finished**, so only relevant matches appear per tab. Finished games automatically move to the "Finished" category. This also includes showing **final scores** on completed match cards.
2. **Date Filter Fix** — The date window dropdown panel is not easily accessible; it needs to be redesigned so it's always visible inline (not hidden behind a dropdown trigger that requires multiple clicks).

---

## API Feasibility & Token Impact Assessment

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Can the Sports API deliver final scores?**
> The `predictorMatches` table stores `startTime` (epoch ms). The current data sources (betwatch.fr + scraper agents) do **not** yet populate a `finalScore` field. However, the schema allows `oddsSnapshot: v.optional(v.any())` as a free-form field. The correct approach is:
> - Add `finalScore: v.optional(v.any())` to `predictorMatches` in `schema.ts`.
> - Add a public `saveMatchResult` mutation that the scraper/orchestrator can call.
> - Add an `updateMatchResult` mutation users/admin can call manually to record scores.
> - The "Finished" tab classification is **100% client-side** using the existing `startTime` vs `now` comparison (no additional API calls needed).

> [!NOTE]
> **Token Usage Impact: ZERO additional cost.** 
> - The three tabs are pure **client-side filtering** of already-loaded `matches[]` data. No new Convex queries, no new API calls, no new agent runs.
> - The `finalScore` field update uses a simple Convex mutation (lightweight DB patch).
> - The date filter UI change is purely cosmetic — no data changes.

